$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure A mixture of DMF (2.00 mL,
25.8 mmol) and 10 M KOH (0.500 mL, 5.00 mmol) was heated at reflux for 5
min. The corresponding aryl halide (1.00 mmol) was added and the
resulting mixture was heated for 0.5 h at 95 °C. The mixture was treated
with additional 10 M KOH (0.500 mL, 5.00 mmol) and heated for an
additional 0.5 h. The reaction was monitored by TLC and additional
portions of 10 M KOH (0.500 mL, 5.00 mmol) were added in 0.5-h intervals
until completion was evident. The reaction mixture was then cooled,
diluted with water, and vacuum filtered (for solid products) or extracted
(for product oils) with Et2O (3x). For reaction products that were
extracted, the organic fractions were combined, dried over anhydrous
Na2SO4, and concentrated under reduced pressure to give the final
product. N, N-dimethyl-2, 4-dinitrobenzenamine (Table 2, entry 1). Using
General Procedure A, 2,4-dinitrofluorobenzene (190 mg, 0.130 mL, 1.00
mmol) underwent conversion after stirring for 3 min at 95 °C. The product
crystallized from the reaction mixture and was collected by vacuum
filtration and washed with ice cold water (10.0 mL). 4-(dimethylamino)
benzaldehyde (Table 2, entry 7). Using General Procedure A with three
additional aliquots of 10M KOH (1.50 mL total), 4-fluorobenzaldehyde
(0.120 g, 0.110 mL, 1.00 mmol) underwent conversion after stirring for 6
h at 95 °C. The product crystallized from the reaction mixture and was
collected by vacuum filtration and washed with ice cold water (10.0 mL).
0.132 g (89%) of pure 4-(dimethylamino)benzaldehyde product as a
colorless powder. 1H NMR (CDCl3 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 9.73 (s, 1 H),
7.73 (d, J=8.8 Hz, 2 H), 6.70 (d, J=8.8 Hz, 2 H), 3.07 (s, 6 H).[5]
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM incremental addition of agent in 0.5h intervals in stage 3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM General method for nucleophilic aromatic substitution of aryl fluorides
and chlorides with dimethylamine using hydroxide-assisted decomposition
of N,N-dimethylformamide
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Garcia, Juana; Sorrentino, Jacob; Diller, Emily J.; Chapman, Daniel;
Woydziak, Zachary R.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2016), 46(5), 475-481

